+/*
+ * The three 320x240 framebuffers share the BORDER_HEIGHT-line black bars with
+ * their neighbour: each buffer after the first starts BORDER_HEIGHT lines
+ * before the end of the previous one, so fb1's top bar and fb0's bottom bar
+ * are the same RDRAM, and likewise for fb2/fb1 (Kaze Emanuar, "Mario 64 wastes
+ * SO MUCH MEMORY", 3:31-4:17).
